(6040759, 887443, 83313, '<td valign="top">Neat. Looks like perhaps some cooling fins on something, or perhaps it is just a sculpture.</td>', 'Neat. Looks like perhaps some cooling fins on something, or perhaps it is just a sculpture.', '2010-06-04 14:06:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(6040762, 887322, 83313, '<td valign="top">I found the same thing when I photographed a <a href="//www.flickr.com/photos/yospiff/4495586209/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">similar steam engine</a> from the same perspective. All the steam rained down in front of the train as spots. I almost entered mine in last month''s FS. I cloned most of it out in my own pic, however. I''m very curious if that aspect of your shot will come off to the average voter as what it is, or if they will perceive it as a flaw.</td>', 'I found the same thing when I photographed a similar steam engine from the same perspective. All the steam rained down in front of the train as spots. I almost entered mine in last month''s FS. I cloned most of it out in my own pic, however. I''m very curious if that aspect of your shot will come off to the average voter as what it is, or if they will perceive it as a flaw.', '2010-06-04 14:11:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6040766, 887282, 83313, '<td valign="top">Lots and lots of detail here, perhaps too much for the challenge limits on pixel and file size. I''ll bet this looks really good in a larger size.</td>', 'Lots and lots of detail here, perhaps too much for the challenge limits on pixel and file size. I''ll bet this looks really good in a larger size.', '2010-06-04 14:14:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6040772, 887419, 83313, '<td valign="top">A fun shot, but it does come off as a snapshot. One thing I found recently when I was photographing the "splash day" at a YMCA, was that by using my 250mm lens and a fairly wide aperture, the busy background was nicely blurred and it improved the pics tremendously. Either that, or getting really close to the subject did the trick. Pool shots certainly have their own issues.</td>', 'A fun shot, but it does come off as a snapshot. One thing I found recently when I was photographing the "splash day" at a YMCA, was that by using my 250mm lens and a fairly wide aperture, the busy background was nicely blurred and it improved the pics tremendously. Either that, or getting really close to the subject did the trick. Pool shots certainly have their own issues.', '2010-06-04 14:18:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6040776, 887359, 83313, '<td valign="top">Quirky and interesting to look at. It appears that the two women are chit-chatting and laughing with each other.</td>', 'Quirky and interesting to look at. It appears that the two women are chit-chatting and laughing with each other.', '2010-06-04 14:20:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6040780, 886671, 83313, '<td valign="top">I like this scene overall, though I do find the bottom of the scene seems to be visually heavier with those bright red barges. My eye wants to explore the interesting old houses, but keeps getting dragged down to the bottom. Certainly worth a vote on the positive side, in spite of my nitpick.</td>', 'I like this scene overall, though I do find the bottom of the scene seems to be visually heavier with those bright red barges. My eye wants to explore the interesting old houses, but keeps getting dragged down to the bottom. Certainly worth a vote on the positive side, in spite of my nitpick.', '2010-06-04 14:24:04.000000', NULL, 1),
