(6041113, 885875, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I rally like the geometry here, all of the lines contribute to the image. I really like the colours too - the acidic yellow against the bile green! But most of all I like the pristine composition.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The red thing under the left hand bench - it kind of throws the image out of whack a bit.<br/> <br/>Overall: Very effective. I like it a lot.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I rally like the geometry here, all of the lines contribute to the image. I really like the colours too - the acidic yellow against the bile green! But most of all I like the pristine composition. Critical stuff: The red thing under the left hand bench - it kind of throws the image out of whack a bit. Overall: Very effective. I like it a lot.', '2010-06-04 18:20:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6041116, 887389, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: This is great - an outtake from Missed focus? Certainly good enough to be reserved for the FS. I really like the dynamism here and the way you have captured the loveliness and fun of the day. High sharpness works well here too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not much - there are some conspicuous dark halos around the front of a couple of faces that I might have worked on but other than that I think it is great.<br/> <br/>Overall: A really compelling image - one that you feel as much as look at.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: This is great - an outtake from Missed focus? Certainly good enough to be reserved for the FS. I really like the dynamism here and the way you have captured the loveliness and fun of the day. High sharpness works well here too. Critical stuff: Not much - there are some conspicuous dark halos around the front of a couple of faces that I might have worked on but other than that I think it is great. Overall: A really compelling image - one that you feel as much as look at.', '2010-06-04 18:23:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6041120, 887459, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: What interesting imagery - full of story, though we are left to extrapolate our own script from your title. This image has an organic, uncontrolled, unbounded quality that I like. I often comment that all photographs are contrived, at least through our process of framing. Here, that effect is minimised - the scene is consuming and alive and through that it feels very uncontrived. Does that make any sense at all?<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing<br/> <br/>Overall: This has quite a different feel from most of the images we see. I like that. A lot.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: What interesting imagery - full of story, though we are left to extrapolate our own script from your title. This image has an organic, uncontrolled, unbounded quality that I like. I often comment that all photographs are contrived, at least through our process of framing. Here, that effect is minimised - the scene is consuming and alive and through that it feels very uncontrived. Does that make any sense at all? Critical stuff: Nothing Overall: This has quite a different feel from most of the images we see. I like that. A lot.', '2010-06-04 18:27:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6041121, 887350, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I like unusual portraits, I have a soft spot for them. This one is unusual for a number of reasons - the extreme lighting, the garish coloration, the ''pose'', your POV; combine these together and you offer something which is quite a piece of work. <br/> <br/>Critical stuff: nothing really<br/> <br/>Overall: The more I look a this the more I realise how much work is here and how someone like me could only ever aspire to be able to pull it off. Very good indeed.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I like unusual portraits, I have a soft spot for them. This one is unusual for a number of reasons - the extreme lighting, the garish coloration, the ''pose'', your POV; combine these together and you offer something which is quite a piece of work.  Critical stuff: nothing really Overall: The more I look a this the more I realise how much work is here and how someone like me could only ever aspire to be able to pull it off. Very good indeed.', '2010-06-04 18:32:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6041133, 884327, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Well you''ve certainly managed to pull of an abstraction of this scene, I particularly like the ''wavy'' characteristics in the image. I like the unusual colour palette too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: In my mind there is something missing here; something that moves this picture from subtle and beautiful to something that is a little over-done.  I wish I could give you more of a clue as to why that is but I really can''t put my finger on it. The bright speck certainly doesn''t help.<br/> <br/>Overall: I commend you vision here and I like what this nearly is - perhaps it made it all the way for you (I hope so), but for me, it isn''t pushing my buttons.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Well you''ve certainly managed to pull of an abstraction of this scene, I particularly like the ''wavy'' characteristics in the image. I like the unusual colour palette too. Critical stuff: In my mind there is something missing here; something that moves this picture from subtle and beautiful to something that is a little over-done.  I wish I could give you more of a clue as to why that is but I really can''t put my finger on it. The bright speck certainly doesn''t help. Overall: I commend you vision here and I like what this nearly is - perhaps it made it all the way for you (I hope so), but for me, it isn''t pushing my buttons.', '2010-06-04 18:51:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6041151, 886503, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Wonderful stuff this - it does have a dreamlike quality about it. I really like the soft movement and the toning. The prominence of the curtain makes me wonder if this is a Rachel image but if I had to put money on it I''d say no. The elements that make up the composition are very well located in the frame and it is this positioning and framing that makes the image so successful.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: Excellent image. It won''t do well but I think it should!</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Wonderful stuff this - it does have a dreamlike quality about it. I really like the soft movement and the toning. The prominence of the curtain makes me wonder if this is a Rachel image but if I had to put money on it I''d say no. The elements that make up the composition are very well located in the frame and it is this positioning and framing that makes the image so successful. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: Excellent image. It won''t do well but I think it should!', '2010-06-04 19:08:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(6041156, 886834, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Wow. This is amazing - an image that transcends the normal animal image and becomes something else entirely. It does some things to the viewer''s brain - I like that!<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: This is an amazing scene but it looks a little under-processed; some colour handling or even black and white with a vignette centred on the eye would have offered some good emphasis for your subject(s).<br/> <br/>Overall: Of course it''s a great image and my personal processing preferences don''t get in the way of that. Great shot.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Wow. This is amazing - an image that transcends the normal animal image and becomes something else entirely. It does some things to the viewer''s brain - I like that! Critical stuff: This is an amazing scene but it looks a little under-processed; some colour handling or even black and white with a vignette centred on the eye would have offered some good emphasis for your subject(s). Overall: Of course it''s a great image and my personal processing preferences don''t get in the way of that. Great shot.', '2010-06-04 19:18:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6041166, 886961, 30791, '<td valign="top">Nice timing! Beautiful photo</td>', 'Nice timing! Beautiful photo', '2010-06-04 19:29:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(6041169, 887171, 30791, '<td valign="top">fantastic! A great combination of DPC''s favorite things.</td>', 'fantastic! A great combination of DPC''s favorite things.', '2010-06-04 19:34:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(6041197, 887181, 108069, '<td valign="top">Wonderful shot. To be honest I normally don''t vote in challenges in which I take part, which is why I was surprised I had voted in this one. But I only voted on yours. And I gave it a 3. I must have been wasted, as I don''t remember this at all. Or just a mistake. I''m now giving it a 10, as it''s incredible, and I will now vote on at least 20% so that 10 sticks.</td>', 'Wonderful shot. To be honest I normally don''t vote in challenges in which I take part, which is why I was surprised I had voted in this one. But I only voted on yours. And I gave it a 3. I must have been wasted, as I don''t remember this at all. Or just a mistake. I''m now giving it a 10, as it''s incredible, and I will now vote on at least 20% so that 10 sticks.', '2010-06-04 19:58:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(6041200, 887297, 108069, '<td valign="top">Cool shot.</td>', 'Cool shot.', '2010-06-04 20:00:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6041202, 887268, 108069, '<td valign="top">Too small. You''ve probably heard that, but still. Use all the room you''re given from now on. Excellent photo, but too small. Still giving you a high mark.</td>', 'Too small. You''ve probably heard that, but still. Use all the room you''re given from now on. Excellent photo, but too small. Still giving you a high mark.', '2010-06-04 20:01:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6041204, 886340, 108069, '<td valign="top">Awesome. Truly awesome.</td>', 'Awesome. Truly awesome.', '2010-06-04 20:02:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6041205, 886805, 108069, '<td valign="top">Excellent. Eerie yet sharp. Well done.</td>', 'Excellent. Eerie yet sharp. Well done.', '2010-06-04 20:04:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6041210, 886550, 108069, '<td valign="top">Fantastic. Colors are jumping, super sharp, clouds are ominous. Even the people down on the pavilion. Amazing image.</td>', 'Fantastic. Colors are jumping, super sharp, clouds are ominous. Even the people down on the pavilion. Amazing image.', '2010-06-04 20:07:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(6041211, 887299, 108069, '<td valign="top">Holy. This is awesome.</td>', 'Holy. This is awesome.', '2010-06-04 20:08:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(6041213, 886287, 103032, '<td valign="top">I''ve seen a lot of this model.  Nice portrait, great eye contact.  Like the pose (tilt of the head) and framing of her red hair against the blue tones of the background.  Great bokeh.</td>', 'I''ve seen a lot of this model.  Nice portrait, great eye contact.  Like the pose (tilt of the head) and framing of her red hair against the blue tones of the background.  Great bokeh.', '2010-06-04 20:11:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6041230, 886924, 103032, '<td valign="top">Like the B&amp;W processing.  Nicely framed using the bridge.</td>', 'Like the B&W processing.  Nicely framed using the bridge.', '2010-06-04 20:23:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6041234, 887469, 103032, '<td valign="top">I like the overexposure to highlight and focus on the master and dog.  I also like the use of the foreground trees/leaves to frame the subject.</td>', 'I like the overexposure to highlight and focus on the master and dog.  I also like the use of the foreground trees/leaves to frame the subject.', '2010-06-04 20:25:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(6041249, 884175, 103032, '<td valign="top">Processing gives this a fantasy/dreamy quality.  I like going with the purple/bluish tones.  Great smile on the model, looks like she is enjoying herself.  I''m guessing you''re using a lensbaby with the heart aperture ring; I like it''s use to focus the attention to the face of the model.  Very playful with the hearts.</td>', 'Processing gives this a fantasy/dreamy quality.  I like going with the purple/bluish tones.  Great smile on the model, looks like she is enjoying herself.  I''m guessing you''re using a lensbaby with the heart aperture ring; I like it''s use to focus the attention to the face of the model.  Very playful with the hearts.', '2010-06-04 20:43:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(6041293, 886904, 108069, '<td valign="top">Nice photo. Sharp and clear, which I really appreciate. I will criticize though (not affecting you score at all): It seems like it could be slightly rotated right to get the tower perfectly perpendicular. And maybe some burning on the clouds to make them pop a bit more. It''s advanced editing, so you can do that. I love how it is and am voting high marks, but this is all I could think of to maybe put it over the top awesome.</td>', 'Nice photo. Sharp and clear, which I really appreciate. I will criticize though (not affecting you score at all): It seems like it could be slightly rotated right to get the tower perfectly perpendicular. And maybe some burning on the clouds to make them pop a bit more. It''s advanced editing, so you can do that. I love how it is and am voting high marks, but this is all I could think of to maybe put it over the top awesome.', '2010-06-04 21:52:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6041340, 879353, 40391, '<td valign="top">I feel this might not do too well in this type of challenge. The dog truely does look awesome &amp; comfy but the focus is not there and the composition and lighting doesn''t work for me. This got a 2 from me.</td>', 'I feel this might not do too well in this type of challenge. The dog truely does look awesome & comfy but the focus is not there and the composition and lighting doesn''t work for me. This got a 2 from me.', '2010-06-04 22:48:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6041347, 887410, 83313, '<td valign="top">Now that''s cool looking and very different.<br/> <br/>ETA: Realized what I like about it. It looks like a display of an audio signal.</td>', 'Now that''s cool looking and very different. ETA: Realized what I like about it. It looks like a display of an audio signal.', '2010-06-04 22:50:58.000000', NULL, 1),
