(6044153, 886990, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: On the surface, this is an image that does little to impress - but somehow it really works. the 70''s coloration, the precise composition, the ''casual'' soft focus, the slight vignette - all the features add up and complement each other. Then there is the story - the gender and age ambiguity, thoughts of what is in the woods and the possibilities of the next few minutes in the life of your subject.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: I think this is pretty masterful - for me, you have transcended ''image'' and have moved into story and communication. The technical choices are no accident, for choices they are - each made in deliberate service to the narrative you have crafted. Bravo.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: On the surface, this is an image that does little to impress - but somehow it really works. the 70''s coloration, the precise composition, the ''casual'' soft focus, the slight vignette - all the features add up and complement each other. Then there is the story - the gender and age ambiguity, thoughts of what is in the woods and the possibilities of the next few minutes in the life of your subject. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: I think this is pretty masterful - for me, you have transcended ''image'' and have moved into story and communication. The technical choices are no accident, for choices they are - each made in deliberate service to the narrative you have crafted. Bravo.', '2010-06-07 03:05:38.000000', NULL, 1),
