(6052864, 886934, 112828, '<td valign="top">I gave this an 8.. I loved the earth tones with that bright green and the dark moody nature..<br/> <br/>I think that it suffered because it''s a bit soft and the eye is ?closed?..  Also dark shots don''t seem to do well here as often as bright cheery shots..</td>', 'I gave this an 8.. I loved the earth tones with that bright green and the dark moody nature.. I think that it suffered because it''s a bit soft and the eye is ?closed?..  Also dark shots don''t seem to do well here as often as bright cheery shots..', '2010-06-12 21:45:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(6052880, 886934, 23317, '<td valign="top">I only voted about 25% in this challenge, and thus I did not vote on the image.  However, I agree with Cory below.  I constantly get dinged in challenges because my shots are darker than most seem to like during voting.  So that''s a choice of whether to pander to the voters or do what you like.<br/> <br/>I think the other reason may be the soft focus.  My eye is drawn to two places on the image. 1) To the bright, mid-body spot above his left leg, and 2) to the spot on the log just below his left leg.  Because of the shallow DOF, that spot on the log appears to be fairly sharp.  But a few inches back, on his eye, the focus appears to be a little softer.  I want to look at his face, but the other two spots draw me away from his face.<br/> <br/>Personally, I very much like the seemingly selective desat.  I can tell that wasn''t done, but like the monotone color against the bright color of the frog.</td>', 'I only voted about 25% in this challenge, and thus I did not vote on the image.  However, I agree with Cory below.  I constantly get dinged in challenges because my shots are darker than most seem to like during voting.  So that''s a choice of whether to pander to the voters or do what you like. I think the other reason may be the soft focus.  My eye is drawn to two places on the image. 1) To the bright, mid-body spot above his left leg, and 2) to the spot on the log just below his left leg.  Because of the shallow DOF, that spot on the log appears to be fairly sharp.  But a few inches back, on his eye, the focus appears to be a little softer.  I want to look at his face, but the other two spots draw me away from his face. Personally, I very much like the seemingly selective desat.  I can tell that wasn''t done, but like the monotone color against the bright color of the frog.', '2010-06-12 22:08:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(6053153, 887230, 66635, '<td valign="top">You were absolutely robbed!  How the hell does a woman kissing a baby''s toes beat lightning striking an erupting volcano??????  I''d score this a 15!</td>', 'You were absolutely robbed!  How the hell does a woman kissing a baby''s toes beat lightning striking an erupting volcano??????  I''d score this a 15!', '2010-06-13 05:14:35.000000', NULL, 0),
